":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-25T21:57:53Z","updated_at":"2026-07-25T21:57:53Z","body":"Apologies that they are unusually longwinded! I was simply trying to cover my bases and explain *why* I think these changes have merit. I'm mostly used to the Proposals repository, where making a strong case for why this is important feels mandatory, otherwise small quality-of-life changes (similar to these documentation notes in my opinion) are quickly disregarded as unnecessary bloat.\r\n\r\nIf that isn't important for documentation changes, I'll definitely keep them shorter next time!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5080742525/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5081437389","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121753#issuecomment-5081437389","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121753","id":5081437389,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLuCUzQ","user":{"login":"skyace65","id":6080368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwODAzNjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6080368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65","html_url":"https://github.com/skyace65","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T01:41:52Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T01:43:59Z","body":"@Arecher I'm a bit confused here. The change we merged from you yesterday in the documentation repository had a brief description (which was good) which nobody gave you any issues for, but I'm also seeing the same kind of long descriptions in your other documentation repository PRs that were opened after that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5081437389/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5081574358","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121753#issuecomment-5081574358","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121753","id":5081574358,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLuKr1g","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T02:14:56Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T02:28:08Z","body":"@skyace65 I wasn't referring to any trouble specifically, especially not recently. But generally over the years with occasional proposals or issues, I just found that you really need to make a strong case for why this is relevant or a good addition.\r\n\r\nMy previous documentation change was a simple outdated variable name, which is something that everyone can agree on needs to be changed, so there was no need to 'justify' anything. With (some) of the documentation changes I made yesterday, it felt like there would be a higher chance users (especially those that are super familiar with how the engine works), believing that the additions are an over-explanation or a non-issue. In other cases there were certain uncertainties about the clarity of my explanations, which I thought were worth pointing to, so they could be double-checked or added to by someone with a more thorough understanding. I'll try to only update documentation when I'm pretty certain of how something works, but I don't have the behind-the-scenes knowledge that many of the maintainers and other contributors do. On top of that I guess I wanted to be careful and thorough, since these are my first contributions and I'm not entirely familiar yet with the general practices!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5081574358/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5083568905","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121753#issuecomment-5083568905","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121753","id":5083568905,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLwEbCQ","user":{"login":"skyace65","id":6080368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwODAzNjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6080368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65","html_url":"https://github.com/skyace65","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skyace65/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T12:57:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T12:57:43Z","body":"@Arecher I understand. Generally speaking for documentation only changes, and this applies to the doc repository as well as the engine one, you don't need to do explanations this in depth. Just give a brief overview over what you're changing and why. Again, what you had in the documentation repository PR was perfect. Longer descriptions can add to review time, and if anyone has any questions they will let you know during review. We don't close documentation PRs because we're confused by something without first asking the author of the PR for clarification.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5083568905/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5105142392","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121753#issuecomment-5105142392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121753","id":5105142392,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMEpKeA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-28T14:02:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T14:03:56Z","body":"After applying ATS's suggestion, could you squash your commits? See our [pull request guidelines](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/organization/pull_requests/creating_pull_requests.html#the-interactive-rebase) for more information","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5105142392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5116676796","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121753#issuecomment-5116676796","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121753","id":5116676796,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMPpKvA","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T10:43:58Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T10:44:58Z","body":"I could not select the remote branch in Git, due to the naming I presume, which means I could not make a local variant to rebase. I renamed the branch so I could actually target it, but in that process this got automatically closed. I similarly cannot target the branch to force push to either. I tried with quotes and doublequotes.\r\n\r\nIs there a way to switch which branch is used for this PR, or should I just make a new one?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5116676796/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5116690052","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121753#issuecomment-5116690052","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121753","id":5116690052,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMPp-hA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T10:45:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T10:45:16Z","body":"Switching branches is not possible so it'd require making a new PR if the name is a problem, I'd suggest using github desktop but otherwise it'd be the solution","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5116690052/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5116749063","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121753#issuecomment-5116749063","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121753","id":5116749063,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMPtlBw","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T10:51:03Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T11:08:42Z","body":"Is Github Desktop an alternative to just using Git? I didn't see any alternatives mentioned on the tutorial page.\r\n\r\nI think I'll make a new PR, getting an learning another tool just isn't worth the trouble anymore, the branch is already squashed.\r\n\r\nEdit, it actually wasn't. The Git showed the right commits I believe, and I squashed them, but on pushing commits from a different PR were the only ones that got added. This was agony. I just remade the changes, that is 10000% easier.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5116749063/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]